# cableunpack

- Label: Cable Unpack
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 2 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cableunpack.html
- Summary (EN): Splits a cable into its individual wires, which are then processed separately; usually placed after Cable Pack. The wires named in Fields are output on output#. Available since version 21.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud cableunpack extrait les fils individuels d'un câble, à l'inverse de cablepack.

- Inputs meaning: ["cable: the input cable to extract wires from"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Set Fields from Input", "meaning": "Fills the Fields parameters with the wires of the input cable"}, {"name": "Fields", "meaning": "Number of wires to extract"}, {"name": "Name", "meaning": "Name of the wire to extract, chosen from the input cable's wires"}, {"name": "Index", "meaning": "Distinguishes wires sharing a name; first instance is 0"}, {"name": "Type", "meaning": "Data type of the wire; affects the node signature"}]

- Caveats: ["Wires are identified by name; Index tells apart wires that share a name"]

